# snap_demo — Inputs

7 input(s) across 3 group(s). 7 carry a tooltip.

Generated by `scripts/input_inventory.py` — do not edit by hand.

## Settings

| Setting | Type | Default | Range | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Length | int | `14` | 1 … 2000 | Lookback in bars. Higher is smoother and slower to react; lower reacts sooner and gives more false turns. |
| Source | source | `close` | — | Which price each bar contributes. close is the convention; hlc3 is steadier on noisy symbols. |

## Appearance

| Setting | Type | Default | Range | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Theme | string | `Dark` | choice | Match this to your chart. Pine cannot read the chart's theme, so getting it wrong is what produces dark text on a dark panel. |
| Show Dashboard | bool | `true` | — | Hides the panel without disabling any calculation. |
| Dashboard Position | string | `Top Right` | choice | Move the panel when it covers price, or when a second script has already taken this corner. |
| Dashboard Transparency | int | `15` | 0 … 90 | 0 is opaque. Past about 60 the candles behind the panel start winning and the numbers stop being readable. |

## Debug/Test

| Setting | Type | Default | Range | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Test Mode | bool | `false` | — | Runs the in-script assertions and shows their pass/fail counts. Leave OFF when publishing — the release bundle blocks on it. |
